To calculate the natural logarithm of a given number x, we can use the Taylor series expansion of the natural logarithm function. The Taylor series expansion for ln(x) is given by:

ln(x) = (x - 1) - (1/2)(x - 1)^2 + (1/3)(x - 1)^3 - (1/4)(x - 1)^4 + ...

We can use this series expansion to calculate the natural logarithm of x with the desired precision.

